L0214: Unreachable match arm

An earlier arm already handles every value this arm could match. Duplicate constructor arms and arms after an exhaustive wildcard are rejected. Remove or reorder the overlapping arm without changing the intended coverage.

Example from `tests/corpus/reject/unreachable_arm.lc`; the full file is a regression test.

```rust
// Arms that are never reached: a variant twice, and `_` after every variant.
enum Light {
    Red,
    Green,
}

fn twice(light: Light) -> bool {
    match light {
        Light::Red => false,
        Light::Red => true,
        Light::Green => true,
    }
}

fn after_all(light: Light) -> bool {
    match light {
        Light::Red => false,
        Light::Green => true,
        _ => true,
    }
}
```

Language, as built: [1.7:5](../../atlas.html#/doc/language/spec-1.7:5).
